From: apklayer
Subject: ANGLE: avoid swapchain present fences on NVIDIA Android WSI

AIDA64 on NVIDIA Android WSI reports VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY from vkGetFenceStatus in WindowSurfaceVk::cleanUpPresentHistory, followed by
VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST and EGL_CONTEXT_LOST. Disable VK_EXT_swapchain_maintenance1 for this path so ANGLE tracks present completion with queue serials
instead of querying present fences created for the Android-loader swapchain.

--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
@@ -6489,7 +6489,7 @@
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, supportsSwapchainMaintenance1,
                             mSwapchainMaintenance1Features.swapchainMaintenance1 == VK_TRUE &&
-                                useVulkanSwapchain == UseVulkanSwapchain::Yes);
+                                useVulkanSwapchain == UseVulkanSwapchain::Yes && !(IsAndroid() && isNvidia));

     // ANI crashes on NVIDIA/Wayland on a swapchain with deferred memory allocation.
     // http://anglebug.com/499347835
     // Keyed on the window system this display resolved to, so it covers the
